# Files that stay in the repository but must not be published to the Comfy
# registry. `comfy node publish` packages every git-tracked file by default:
#   https://docs.comfy.org/registry/publishing
#
# dev/ is the test suite and the browser harnesses. It has no business in an
# installed node pack, and dev/tests/test_standards.py in particular is a table
# of every literal the registry's scanner searches for -- publishing it means
# publishing the bait. 2.3.0 and 2.3.2 both shipped it and both came back
# flagged.
dev/

# docs/ is the repository's own documentation -- design notes, the technical
# write-up, and docs/images/ which now holds a screenshot of every node for the
# README. GitHub renders all of it; nobody installing the pack needs any of it.
# It was 1.2 MB of the 1.88 MB published for 2.5.0, and the node screenshots
# would have taken the archive past 9 MB.
#
# web/docs/ is a DIFFERENT folder and must keep shipping: it is the per-node
# help ComfyUI shows inside the app. Only the top-level docs/ is excluded here.
docs/

# Transcription and lyric scoring are held back from this release. The code
# stays in the repository -- it is finished work and comes back in a later
# version -- but it is not registered in __init__.py and is not published, so
# the archive carries no module for a node that does not exist. Holding them
# back also takes `transformers` and `demucs` out of the shipped tree entirely,
# which are the pack's only heavyweight optional imports.
transcribe/
viewers/nova_lyric_report_viewer.py
web/nova_lyric_report_viewer.js
web/docs/NovaAudioTranscribe/
web/docs/NovaLyricScore/
web/docs/NovaLyricReportViewer/

# The workflow PNGs are drag-to-load templates: each one embeds the same graph
# its .json sibling holds, so publishing both ships every workflow twice. They
# are 4.8 MB of a 7.5 MB archive. The .json files DO ship -- an installed pack
# still has every workflow -- and the PNGs stay in git so GitHub can show them.
example_workflows/*/*.png

# training/RELEASE_NOTES.md is a handover document written for whoever prepares
# the next registry build -- it opens "For the agent preparing ..." and narrates
# revisions, including nodes held back from this release. It is working material,
# not user documentation, and the same reasoning that keeps docs/ out keeps it out.
training/RELEASE_NOTES.md
